{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And now, put off your ornaments from upon you.</b> These are the garments upon which the blood of the covenant was sprinkled — and it is the blood of the offerings that the firstborn sacrificed at Sinai. They were called עדי (ornament) for Israel, a splendor and great glory, in that the blood upon them was a sign and token of their acceptance of the covenant of the Holy One, blessed be He. I have already mentioned this in the section ואלה המשפטים, and it is the opinion of our master Ḥananel, of blessed memory. Since they have now denied the deed of the calf, that covenant was annulled, and He commanded them to strip them off; and this is ״ויתנצלו בני ישראל את עדיהם״ — it tells that they did as the Almighty said and stripped off their garments. And what it says above, ״ולא שתו איש עדיו עליו״, is as if it said 'all his ornaments' — to say that of their own accord they refrained: no one put on all his ornaments, but only some of his ornaments. But now, when they were commanded by the Almighty ״הורד עדיך״, they removed all the ornament entirely and stripped it from themselves." "<b>And according to</b> what the Sages, of blessed memory, interpreted — that this 'עדי' was the Explicit Name — the explanation of the verses is: ״ולא שתו איש עדיו״ — their actual garments; ״הורד עדיך״ — it is the ornament of the Explicit Name. Therefore it did not say הפשט עדיך (strip off your ornaments) but the language of הורד (put down) and the language of מעליך (from upon you): for they descended from that elevation, and that rank was removed from them. And likewise the Sages, of blessed memory, interpreted: ״זינאות חגר להון״ — 'they girded weapons upon themselves,' and it is the weapon of the Explicit Name that was in their hands from Mount Horeb; as they interpreted (Exodus 32:16): ״חרות על הלחת״ — חֵרוּת (freedom) from the Angel of Death, for they had the names of the Holy One, blessed be He, in their hands and death could not prevail over them. To this Onkelos alluded by translating ״תיקון זיניהון״, and this is the meaning of ״ויתנצלו בני ישראל את עדיהם מהר חורב״ — that ornament which they had from Mount Horeb. Therefore Onkelos translated ״הורד אעדי״ in the sense of removing power; and likewise ״ויתנצלו ואעדיאו״. The intention is to say that those elevated qualities and luminations that each and every one possessed, like the ministering angels, from Mount Horeb — they were removed and lost from them, and Moses took them. And this is what it juxtaposes: ״ומשה יקח את האהל״, from the language of (Job 29:3) ״בהלו נרו״, and likewise (Numbers 24:5) ״מה טובו אהליך״, as I shall explain there with the help of the Almighty." "<b>And I have already</b> explained in the section ואלה המשפטים why the Torah mentioned the great distinction of this ornament now, when it was lost from them, and did not mention it at the Giving of the Torah when they merited it."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :register {:flags {0 ["the Almighty"], 1 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:46.439129485Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}